await writeFile(L23+'notes.md',`l23 is a diagnostic. l21 remains the accepted base. None of l22 is retained.\n\nMCPS supplies measured regional stellar colors. The full release has ${num(input.rows).toLocaleString('en-US')} rows; ${num(input.qualityRows).toLocaleString('en-US')} pass common BVI cuts. The unresolved-light estimate uses deeper HST bar and disc fields. Colors are smoothed at 150 pc.\n\n| Masked bar close-up | R/G | B/G |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n${row('Horálek',photo,'bar')}\n${row('l21',old,'bar')}\n${row('l23',model,'bar')}\n\nThe bar errors are ${error.map(v=>(100*v).toFixed(2)+'%').join(' and ')}. The combined core and edge color error falls by ${improvement.toFixed(1)}%, but B/G still has the wrong gradient: the core is less blue than the edges. This fails the intended acceptance test.\n\nNative training and held-out RMS are ${num(m.trainRelativeRms).toFixed(6)} and ${num(m.heldoutRelativeRms).toFixed(6)}, versus 0.257606 and 0.309402 for l21. Outer light is ${outer.toFixed(1)}% high. RMS is reported, not used as the gate.\n\nThe side views retain the l21 volume and heights, with no new line-of-sight extrusion. They have overly red outskirts because the old-disc grade reaches its green and blue lower bounds. All geometry, dust, catalogue amplitudes and resolved fractions remain at l21. Three calibration trials were completed; the third repaired the outskirts but worsened the bar gradient.\n\nThe input pass took 74.3 seconds. The tiny and small projections took about 24 and 239 seconds; later color trials reused those exact projections. No full-resolution fit or slab bake ran.\n\nSee method.md for sources, measured versus estimated light, and the Gaia check.\n`);
const gaia=rec(q.gaiaCheck),core=rec(gaia.core),edges=rec(gaia.edges);
await writeFile(L23+'method.md',`The color field comes from [MCPS, Zaritsky et al. 2004](https://doi.org/10.1086/423910), using the [CDS release](https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/ftp/J/AJ/128/1606/ReadMe). Native right ascension is in hours; TAP uses degrees. Missing bands remain missing. The catalogue covers the main optical body, not the distant outskirts.\n\nCommon BVI measurements use 13.5 ≤ V < 20 and uncertainties at most 0.15 mag. U is not used for grading because the paper reports calibration and scan systematics. Saturated bright stars are excluded. Fluxes are summed before ratios; magnitudes are never averaged. [SVO filter zero points](https://svo2.cab.inta-csic.es/theory/fps/) convert Vega magnitudes to F_nu proxies. Red is interpolated between V and Cousins I.\n\nGaia DR3 random-index astrometry supplies a statistical foreground estimate, following the retained [Luri et al. selection](https://arxiv.org/html/2012.01771). The high-parallax stars excluded from the old calibration query are restored before estimating contamination. There are 35,791 MCPS/Gaia matches within one arcsecond. This is statistical membership, with an extrapolation beyond the Gaia calibration magnitude limit.\n\nFaint light comes from [Holtzman, Afonso and Dolphin 2006](https://doi.org/10.1086/507074) and the [author archive](http://astronomy.nmsu.edu/holtz/archival/html/lg.html), reduction phot-2.03. The bar field is lmc_u2o901; the disc field is lmc_u2c501. Published artificial-star experiments correct V/I recovery. Faint light is normalized to regional MCPS V = 18.5–20 light. B follows the measured MCPS color locus. The extrapolated faint tail is an assumption, with a geometric ratio bounded between 0.2 and 0.8. The bar field has a published aperture-correction warning. No absolute HST color zero point is transferred: faint/reference flux ratios are used. Residual inter-chip systematics remain.\n\n| Check | Bar core | Bar edges |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| MCPS B−V, resolved plus estimated faint light | ${num(core.mcpsWithEstimatedUnresolvedBMinusV).toFixed(3)} | ${num(edges.mcpsWithEstimatedUnresolvedBMinusV).toFixed(3)} |\n| Gaia integrated BP−RP | ${num(core.gaiaIntegratedBpMinusRp).toFixed(3)} | ${num(edges.gaiaIntegratedBpMinusRp).toFixed(3)} |\n| Estimated unresolved fraction of V light | ${(100*num(core.estimatedUnresolvedFractionV)).toFixed(1)}% | ${(100*num(edges.estimatedUnresolvedFractionV)).toFixed(1)}% |\n\nBoth surveys indicate a bluer core. The bands and magnitude selections differ, so their numerical colors are not expected to match. Gaia is not independent of the foreground selection. The displayed model fails to preserve the full blue trend despite this agreement in the inputs.\n\nRegional colors attach to body-plane coordinates in the existing l21 populations. They are conditionally dereddened using the retained mixed dust layer before the canonical renderer attenuates them. Distances, thicknesses, density, warp, dust, positions and point photometry are unchanged. Green-light projections before the grade agree to floating-point precision. Only six global RGB coefficients vary; no coefficient is fitted separately by region or pixel.\n\nThe third calibration trial added an outer-annulus color constraint and a stronger brightness constraint. It fixed the red outskirts but worsened the bar gradient, so the second trial is preserved as the final diagnostic. The lower-bound old-disc colors show that the global component calibration remains degenerate. This result is not promoted over l21.\n`);
await writeFile(ROOT+'src/objects/lmc-volume/.local/CURRENT-WORK.md',`# Current LMC work\n\nl23 is complete as a diagnostic, starting from the owner-accepted l21.\nNo l22 density, grain or dust changes are retained.\nThe mean bar color passes 2 percent, but the blue core-to-edge trend fails.\nThe bar regional color error improves by ${improvement.toFixed(1)} percent.\nOuter light is 11.8 percent high, and the side views have red outskirts.\nl21 remains the accepted base. Three calibration trials are preserved.\n\nMCPS supplies regional BVI flux colors, smoothed at 150 pc.\nThe complete release contains 24,107,002 stars; 6,599,348 pass common BVI cuts.\nA Gaia astrometric sample estimates foreground contamination.\nTwo deeper HST fields estimate unresolved light, with artificial-star corrections.\nThe missing faint B light and tail remain estimates, clearly separated from MCPS measurements.\nAll l21 geometry, dust, catalogue objects, grain fractions and density remain unchanged.\n\n## Reusable inputs and evidence\n\n- versions/l23/inputs/ contains the native MCPS release, queries, HST photometry and artificial stars.\n- versions/l23/mcps-material.json and the four mcps color fields preserve the measured material.\n- versions/l23/regional-flux.json separates resolved and estimated faint light.\n- versions/l23/cache/ contains the exact completed projections.\n- versions/l23/ contains the sheet, l21 comparison, bar crop, notes and qualification.\n- versions/l23/round1/ and round3/ preserve rejected alternatives.\n- versions/l21/ remains the accepted structure and completeness correction.\n- versions/l20/, l19/, l13/, l12/ and l11/ retain Gaia, HERITAGE and catalogue inputs.\n- archive/ retains Bell, VMC, SMASH, warp data and research.\n- ../source/preparation/l23/ contains the version records and non-promotion verdict.\n\nA local version commit is authorized. No push, PR, R2 publication or message is authorized.\nNo further model fit, render or training process is running.\n`);
